        "line": 11,
        "location": "design.md#Decision: The export loads every event, then writes the CSV",
        "raisedBy": [
          "performance"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Stream the export: read the rows with a server-side cursor or keyset batches on (org_id, created_at, id), turn each batch into CSV lines and write them to the response stream with backpressure, so memory stays bounded by the batch size whatever the log's size. This keeps the spec's \"every event, oldest first\" unchanged. The same streaming also fixes the event-loop stall: with the rows and the CSV built in one synchronous `map`/`join`, the instance's single event loop (design.md#Context) serves no other request until the whole string is built. Select only the columns the CSV needs instead of `SELECT *`. Record the streaming choice and its rejected alternative under \"Alternatives considered\".",
